# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> restore the INTERNAL 'golden' snapshot: X (-nocursor) +
# VICE xpet at the PET 2001's own untouched cold power-on screen. Nothing is
# curated into the fixture and nothing is typed after the restore: the oldest
# machine in the gallery is shown exactly as it woke up in 1977, and the
# affordances (the type-in demo, the on-screen keyboard) live in the SPA around
# it. Rationale: plus4's first golden rested deep inside an application and was
# rejected on the exhibit floor.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore PET 2001 (1977) at its own untouched cold power-on screen: "*** COMMODORE BASIC *** / 7167 BYTES FREE / READY." in blue-white on black, 40x25 characters drawn double-size (-CRTCdsize) by VICE xpet -model 2001 as a 768x532 SDL window on an 800x600 X root. VICE's model 2001 is the 1977 original and not a badge: RamSize=8, Crtc=0 (the machine predates the 6545 CRTC every later PET used), VideoSize=40, KeyboardType=4 (the chiclet graphics keyboard), palette 2001-blueish.vpl. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; PET CB2 sound -> ALSA -> AC97 (the 1977 machine shipped with no sound hardware at all, so this is silent in practice).

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
# Four frames each way. The frame-derived two-frame figure is a FLOOR, not an
# answer: 40/40 was bisected on vic20 (scripts/dev/emu-key-pacing-bisect.py) and
# still corrupted 1 line in 22 under host scheduling stalls, while 80/80 lost
# nothing in 22. Same emulator, same host, so this tile ships 80/80 as well, and
# scripts/build-guests/pet2001.sh types its whole demo program at exactly this
# rate as part of the build proof. The SPA typist must therefore budget at least
# 160 ms per character (registry spa.demoProgram.perCharMs=180); below the drain
# rate a backlog builds and BASIC loses characters while it is tokenising.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
# No SH_KEY_MAP: VICE's default SDL symbolic keymap for the graphics keyboard
# (sdl_grus_sym.vkm) already maps host ASCII onto the PET matrix. Proven on this
# tile by typing the whole demo listing, including $ ( ) * + , which the PET
# 2001's chiclet keyboard places nothing like a PC does. Letters must be sent
# UNSHIFTED (registry keyboard.letterCase=upper-only): unshifted PET keys give
# upper-case glyphs and SHIFT gives the graphics set.
